# What `dart pub publish` leaves out of the archive.
#
# IMPORTANT: pub ignores a directory's .gitignore when that directory has a
# .pubignore, so this file cannot just list the extras — it has to repeat
# everything .gitignore excludes as well. Keep the two in sync.

# --- Not shipped, and the reason this file exists --------------------------
#
# README media. The README links these by absolute raw.githubusercontent.com
# URL, so they render on GitHub and on pub.dev without being downloaded by
# every `pub get`. The animation alone is 9 MB against a ~100 KB lib/.
media/

# The example app is a full Flutter app with its own iOS and Android projects.
# pub.dev links to it on GitHub; shipping it would dwarf the package.
#
# Its README is the one exception. `example/README.md` is the first candidate
# pana looks for when deciding whether a package has an example, which is worth
# 10 pub points, and pub.dev renders it as the Example tab. Note the pattern:
# excluding `example/` itself would stop pub descending into the directory, so
# the negation below could never re-include anything.
example/*
!example/README.md

# Local verification notes and the Phase 0 research record. Useful in the
# repository, not to a consumer.
docs/

# --- Repeated from .gitignore ---------------------------------------------

